      "narration": "Two athletes step onto the mat. Same height, same weight, same training. They fight, and it's close, the kind that could go either way. And then one of them wins. Now watch what happens if we rewind, swap the color of their gear, and run it back. The winner might change. Not the fighting, just the color. Same two people, same moves, and a different hand gets raised. I first ran into this on a test, of all places. A reading passage claimed the color you wear can change who wins, and who loses. It sounded like nonsense. It isn't. And it goes a lot deeper than sports.",
