      "narration": "In 2004, two researchers went looking. They pulled the results from four combat sports at the Athens Olympics. Boxing, taekwondo, and two kinds of wrestling. And here's the crucial part, in these sports, the gear is handed out at random. Red or blue, nobody picks. It's a coin flip. So if color did nothing, red should win half the time. It didn't. Red won fifty-five percent of bouts. And in the closest fights, the ones that could tip either way, red won sixty-two. A coin that lands red sixty-two percent of the time isn't a fair coin. Something was loading it.",
