    {
      "narration": "And once you know to look for it, you start seeing it everywhere. Years earlier, researchers dug through penalty records in pro football and hockey. Teams that wore black got penalized more, not occasionally, but consistently. Two teams even changed their jerseys to black one season, and their penalties jumped right after. Now, maybe players in black really do play dirtier. So the researchers filmed the exact same plays, once in white, once in black. Referees called the black version more aggressive. Red flatters you to the judge, and black incriminates you. Either way, they're not scoring what you did. They're scoring what you wore.",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "And once you know to look for it, you start seeing it everywhere.",
